      "exam_slot": "Q22",
      "title": "Interior and exterior angle reasoning",
      "statement": "a) Prove and use the Polygon Interior Angles Sum Theorem. b) Find and use the sum of exterior angles of a polygon.",
      "rule_summary": "For a convex polygon, diagonals from one vertex form n − 2 triangles. Interior sum = (n − 2)180°. One exterior angle at each vertex, taken consistently around the polygon, sums to 360°.",
